<?php

/**
 * The correct signatures for str_contains() and str_starts_with().
 *
 * PHPStan reads the entries in composer's autoload_files for symbol
 * discovery, and mockery/mockery ships PHP 8.0 polyfills there:
 *
 *     vendor/mockery/mockery/library/helpers.php
 *
 *     // @param non-empty-string $haystack
 *     // @param non-empty-string $needle
 *     function str_contains(string $haystack, string $needle): bool
 *
 * Those docblocks are wrong on both counts — both functions accept an
 * empty haystack and an empty needle, and PHP's own signatures say so —
 * but PHPStan has no way to know the declaration is a polyfill, and
 * prefers it over the native signature. The result was four call sites
 * across Reach being reported as passing the wrong type to functions
 * they were calling correctly.
 *
 * The polyfill bodies never even run: they are guarded by
 * function_exists() and this plugin's floor is PHP 8.1, where both are
 * native. So the fix is to correct the signatures rather than to silence
 * the call sites, which is why this is a stub and not an ignoreErrors
 * entry — the latter would have to be repeated for every future call and
 * would still be describing the symptom.
 *
 * <b>Arrived with mockery 1.6.13.</b> 1.6.12 shipped no such polyfill, so
 * this was invisible until the bump; the failure looks like a PHPStan
 * regression and is not one.
 *
 * Promises carries the same stub for str_contains alone — see
 * promises/phpstan/str-contains.stub. This one covers str_starts_with
 * too, because Reach calls it.
 *
 * Removable once mockery/mockery drops the polyfills or fixes the
 * annotations.
 */

/**
 * @param string $haystack
 * @param string $needle
 */
function str_contains(string $haystack, string $needle): bool
{
}

/**
 * @param string $haystack
 * @param string $needle
 */
function str_starts_with(string $haystack, string $needle): bool
{
}
